# reorder: units that gave their order up are ordered again. Two corridors 8 cells wide, each plugged wall to wall
# by four of the player's own idle bodies; six bodies are sent through each at tick 2 and give their orders up
# before the plug (the stand-down, about tick 1,200).
#   A  the plug is ordered away at tick 2,000 and the six are sent to the same point again at tick 2,600: all six
#      arrive.
#   B  the six are sent again at tick 1,600 while the plug still stands (they give up again: no loop, no twitch),
#      and a third time at tick 3,400 after the plug left at 3,000: all six arrive.
# At start offset 1 some of the 2x2 bodies begin on origins the static plane rejects and walk off them (the walk
# off an illegal origin, Member::escapeTo). One of them reached its legal origin in its own update and was moved on
# by another body's swap in the same tick; the walk's record, cleared only by the body's own next update, then
# named an origin two cells from the body, and TAK_LEGION_VERIFY aborted at tick 3,507 ("a walk off an illegal
# origin aims past its neighbours"). The record now ends with the walk, and with any step another rule gives the
# body. ctest legion_reorder runs this file under the hook.
# Keys: g.A.arrived, g.B.arrived (6 each), work.escape_steps.total (0, 11, 15 at offsets 0, 1, -1).
scn 1
name reorder
ticks 6000
seed 7
players 1
weapons off
map flat 128 64
wall 34 0 60 16
wall 34 24 60 16
wall 34 48 60 16
type m mover 2 2500 10 1.79999
group P1 0 m 4 cells 61,17 61,19 61,21 61,23
group P2 0 m 4 cells 61,41 61,43 61,45 61,47
group A 0 m 6 rect 4 14 12 26 pitch=3
group B 0 m 6 rect 4 38 12 50 pitch=3
at 2 move A 112 20
at 2000 move P1 20 6
at 2600 move A 112 20
at 2 move B 112 44
at 1600 move B 112 44
at 3000 move P2 20 58
at 3400 move B 112 44
